<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Description>What the device pieces read from an experiment, for a workflow that makes no experiment folder (a calibration, a preflight), in place of LaunchSettings and LogLabExperiment: PathPrefix, declared and never published, so no piece's log starts and nothing is written under rig.yml's rootPath; and SubjectId from Start, the property SubjectId, a name that is no mouse's (such as _valve-calibration_), so LickSpoutStage's in positions are rig.yml's lickSpoutDefaultPosition. Included once, with neither LogLabExperiment nor LaunchSettings, and the workflow declares neither subject itself (no_experiment_folder_problems).</Description>
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SubjectId" Description="The subject the pieces see: a name that is no mouse's, such as _valve-calibration_, so no mouse's spout positions are read or saved." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
          <Value />
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
        <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
          <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
        </Combinator>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
        <Name>SubjectId</Name>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:String">
        <rx:Name>PathPrefix</rx:Name>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
